The complete unified Jacobian mixed-addition formula in coordinates.rs follows
Brier & Joye (PKC 2002) as formulated in bitcoin-core/secp256k1 (MIT License),
scaled by s = 2 to avoid field halving. Distinct Jacobian mixed addition
follows Bernstein & Lange (madd-2007-bl).

The homogeneous complete mixed-addition formula retained for batch normalization
tests in coordinates.rs is adapted from RustCrypto k256 0.13.4
src/arithmetic/projective.rs (Renes-Costello-Batina 2015, Algorithm 8).
